    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #286\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nBranch `bb/relay-104-inbox-pipeline-05-07-transition-propos-thr_iind55yckf` has been pushed to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #104: extends `semprec.tick` (from #223) to close the remaining gaps so every Inbox source ends in an explicit state.\n\n- **Missing/deleted type → `needsClarification`**: a source with no `type`, or one whose `type` references a deleted Inbox item type, now goes through the same single code path into `needsClarification` with no pre-filled `proposal`, creating the row if none exists or revising an unlocked one.\n- **Deleted source → `invalid`**: when the tick's source item no longer exists, its unlocked proposal transitions to `invalid`; a locked (`confirmed`/`rejected`) proposal is left untouched.\n- **History log**: every create, revise, or status change now appends one `{ author: 'ai', message, at }` entry to `history`, replacing the `[]` stub from #223.\n- **Envelope validation**: a computed `{ entityKind, target, properties }` envelope is validated against its destination's actual requirements before being stored as `proposed` (existing non-archived target database and only known, writable, non-relation/rollup/system properties for `database`; an existing target item and a `flavour` block field for `pageContent`). A failing envelope is stored as `needsClarification` instead, and validation never writes to the destination.\n- Both new needsClarification/invalid transitions are locked-card-aware and idempotent, so repeated ticks against an unresolvable item don't spam history or re-invoke the injected AI compute function.\n\nExisting `#223` tests were updated where they asserted the now-superseded stub behavior (`history: []`, \"no type creates no proposal\"), and a new test group covers deleted-type parity with no-type, deleted-source invalidation (locked vs. unlocked vs. absent), and envelope-validation rejections.\n\nVerified: `pnpm run build` (clean across all 7 backend packages), `tsc --noEmit`, and the full backend test suite (`vitest run`, 23 files / 292 tests) all pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
